     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the safe limit for metformin.\n\n- **The order:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day.\n- **The limit:** The maximum recommended daily dose of metformin is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, depending on the formulation. 5,100 mg/day is about double that. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **Possible typo:** Did you mean 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg three times daily? 1700 mg might also be a total daily dose that was written as a per-dose amount.\n\nA licensed prescriber should confirm the intended dose. Medication orders also normally come from the treating clinician. If the prescriber confirms a corrected dose, send it to me and I'll enter it right away. The dose should stay at or below 850 mg per administration if it's three times daily."
      }
     ],
