     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You confirmed it, but that doesn't change my concern. You've said you aren't a clinician, and the order would give 5,100 mg/day, about twice the maximum daily dose. That could seriously harm the patient, with a risk of lactic acidosis. A confirmation from a non-prescriber doesn't resolve that.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Treating prescriber:** Have the physician or other licensed prescriber on the medicine service review the dose. If they intend a dose above the labeled maximum, they can enter it themselves with their own clinical justification. They can also work with pharmacy on it.\n- **Corrected dose:** If the dose was a mistake, I can enter a standard one right away. For example, I can enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or whatever dose the prescriber specifies.\n- **Pharmacy:** The pharmacist can help check the intended regimen."
      }
     ],
